Subject: [PATCH] core/native: release an owned remote FD on connection setup failure

Base: PipeWire 1.6.11, 4287f31510771fc999f8a58a024c81ca10b8d55f

pw_context_connect_fd documents transfer on success and error. core_new can
fail before a protocol client exists, and the native protocol can fail to
register its loop source. Neither branch owns a source capable of closing
the FD. Close it at the respective ownership boundary, preserve the original
error, and clear the protocol connection's borrowed FD before destruction.

The existing local-socket/internal callers do not close after connect_fd
returns an error. Fixed 1.6.11 loop_add_io does not close the caller's FD.
Its get_source has already linked the allocated source before poll setup;
unlink that allocation on failure so later loop teardown cannot follow it.

Upstream a9f62579ba95dd4ac20376a0f2f63455ef73aa45 establishes the same FD
transfer rule globally at loop_add_io. Backporting that semantic change also
requires the multi-module caller adjustments in 894e97aaa58d5ed755f7e7f32d432c22d7d1f73c
and 8907d0860be1dfeeda2b21b0be0adebca26eb87d. This adaptation deliberately
keeps 1.6.11's low-level rule and fixes only the audited remote-FD caller.
No success path or borrowed (do_close=false) FD is changed.

The fixed revision's upstream MIT notices continue to apply. This is a
huhucapture adaptation, not an assertion of upstream acceptance.

diff --git a/src/pipewire/core.c b/src/pipewire/core.c
--- a/src/pipewire/core.c
+++ b/src/pipewire/core.c
@@ -440,8 +440,12 @@
 	int res;
 
 	core = core_new(context, properties, user_data_size);
-	if (core == NULL)
+	if (core == NULL) {
+		res = errno;
+		close(fd);
+		errno = res;
 		return NULL;
+	}
 
 	pw_log_debug("%p: connect fd:%d", core, fd);
 
diff --git a/src/modules/module-protocol-native.c b/src/modules/module-protocol-native.c
--- a/src/modules/module-protocol-native.c
+++ b/src/modules/module-protocol-native.c
@@ -1158,6 +1158,7 @@
 static int impl_connect_fd(struct pw_protocol_client *client, int fd, bool do_close)
 {
 	struct client *impl = SPA_CONTAINER_OF(client, struct client, this);
+	int res;
 
 	impl->connected = false;
 	impl->disconnecting = false;
@@ -1167,8 +1168,13 @@
 					fd,
 					SPA_IO_IN | SPA_IO_OUT | SPA_IO_HUP | SPA_IO_ERR,
 					do_close, on_remote_data, impl);
-	if (impl->source == NULL)
-		return -errno;
+	if (impl->source == NULL) {
+		res = -errno;
+		pw_protocol_native_connection_set_fd(impl->connection, -1);
+		if (do_close)
+			close(fd);
+		return res;
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
diff --git a/spa/plugins/support/loop.c b/spa/plugins/support/loop.c
--- a/spa/plugins/support/loop.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/support/loop.c
@@ -897,6 +897,7 @@
 	return &source->source;
 
 error_exit_free:
+	spa_list_remove(&source->link);
 	free(source);
 	errno = -res;
 error_exit:
